Same pattern as fix-android-support.patch's CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME gates, extended
for Emscripten -- but NOT aliased to LINUX (see below for why that was
tried first and reverted). GNS's own platform detection has a hard
message(FATAL_ERROR "Could not identify your target operating system")
fallthrough in both CMakeLists.txt and src/CMakeLists.txt whenever
CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME isn't one of Linux/Android/Darwin/FreeBSD/Windows --
Emscripten sets CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME to "Emscripten", matching none of them,
so configure failed before a single line of C++ was even compiled
(confirmed via an isolated wasm32 build spike -- see
examples/blam/cblam-testing/WEBRTC_TRANSPORT.md). Gets its own empty
elseif branch in both files, just to avoid the fallthrough.

Also patched here: TARGET_ARCH_FLAGS unconditionally adds -msse2 whenever
CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR matches an x86 pattern -- under the wasm32-emscripten
triplet, CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR still reports the host arch (x86_64), not a
wasm-specific value (a cross-compile toolchain-detection quirk, not GNS's
doing), so GNS believed it should target native x86 SSE2 and passed -msse2
to em++, which errors unless paired with -msimd128/-mrelaxed-simd. Excluded
via CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES Emscripten -- wasm32 has no native SSE2 to
target in the first place, so the flag should never apply here regardless.

First attempt at the CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME gates aliased Emscripten to LINUX
(same macro Android gets), since GNS's own platform macros
(src/public/minbase/minbase_identify.h) don't have a general "unsupported
but keep going" fallback either. That broke worse than it fixed:
IsLinux()-gated code assumes real kernel facilities Emscripten's libc
doesn't have -- sys/ptrace.h (src/tier0/dbg.cpp, debugger-session
detection) and epoll (src/public/tier0/platform_sockets.h, the socket
polling backend) both don't exist under Emscripten, and both are gated on
IsLinux(), not on anything more specific. Given Emscripten's own identity
doesn't need to reuse Linux's for correctness -- IsPosix() alone is enough
for GNS's socket/threading code -- minbase_identify.h gets a real
IsEmscripten() of its own instead:
  - dbg.cpp: same false-return stub Android already has for
    Plat_IsInDebugSession(), since Emscripten has no debugger-session
    concept either. The ptrace.h #include itself is already gated on
    IsLinux(), so once Emscripten stops claiming that, it's skipped for
    free.
  - platform_sockets.h: routed to the same USE_POLL fallback __APPLE__
    already uses instead of USE_EPOLL -- confirmed USE_POLL has a full
    alternate implementation throughout steamnetworkingsockets_lowlevel.cpp
    before relying on it, not just a stub.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 6365a37..91ce12d 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -128,7 +128,7 @@ if(USE_CRYPTO STREQUAL "libsodium")
 endif()
 
 # We always need at least sse2 on x86
-if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "amd64.*|x86_64.*|AMD64.*|i686.*|i386.*|x86.*")
+if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "amd64.*|x86_64.*|AMD64.*|i686.*|i386.*|x86.*" AND NOT CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES Emscripten)
        set(TARGET_ARCH_FLAGS "-msse2")
 endif()
 
@@ -142,6 +142,12 @@ function(set_target_common_gns_properties TGT)
 
     if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES Linux OR CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES Android)
 		target_compile_definitions(${TGT} PUBLIC LINUX)
+	elseif(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES Emscripten)
+		# Deliberately NOT aliased to LINUX: minbase_identify.h gives
+		# Emscripten its own IsEmscripten()/IsPosix() identity instead,
+		# since IsLinux()-gated code (epoll, /proc/self/status ptrace
+		# detection) assumes real kernel facilities Emscripten's libc
+		# doesn't provide.
 	elseif(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES Darwin)
 		target_compile_definitions(${TGT} PUBLIC OSX)
 	elseif(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES FreeBSD)
